.TH AMERIKA-CHANNEL 8 "2026-10-21" "Amerika OS" "Amerika OS Manual"
.SH NAME
amerika\-channel \- choose the Amerika OS update channel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amerika\-channel
.RB [ status | stable | testing ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Amerika OS has two update channels in the signed repository: the
.B stable
channel, which every system uses, and the
.B testing
channel, which receives packages before they are promoted and may break. Testing is disabled by default and is never enabled
by the installer.
.PP
.B amerika\-channel testing
sets
.B Enabled: yes
in
.IR /etc/apt/sources.list.d/amerika\-testing.sources ;
.B stable
sets it back to
.BR no .
Packages from testing are still not installed automatically: the APT pin gives testing a lower priority than the Ubuntu archive;
install from it with
.BR "apt install \-t testing" " " \fIpackage\fR.
Unattended upgrades only ever consider the stable suite. Run
.B apt update
after changing the channel. The command needs root.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/amerika.sources
Stable channel (package amerika\-repo\-keyring).
.TP
.I /etc/apt/preferences.d/amerika.pref
Pins.
.TP
.I /etc/amerika\-os/channel
Name of the selected channel, shown in the message of the day.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt_preferences (5),
.BR sources.list (5),
.BR amerika\-flavour (7)
